input.content:
{
  "name": "starter",
  "spawnLocation": 1,
  "startingItems": [
    "dagger"
  ],
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "dagger",
      "description": "A short, worn blade. Better than nothing.",
      "kind": "weapon",
      "attackBonus": 0,
      "attackDice": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "shortsword",
      "description": "A plain iron shortsword. Too long for a goblin, which is presumably why it was stolen.",
      "kind": "weapon",
      "attackBonus": 1,
      "attackDice": 6
    },
    {
      "name": "long knife",
      "description": "A hand and a half of straight grey blade, sharp yet, with a horn grip worn to the shape of somebody's fingers. It was laid down the length of a body by someone who had further to walk and chose to walk it unarmed.",
      "kind": "weapon",
      "attackBonus": 2,
      "attackDice": 8
    },
    {
      "name": "rusted chisel",
      "description": "A mason's chisel, a foot of iron gone orange with water, the head burred over from being hit a great many times. The edge is still an edge. It was made for taking cut stone out of a wall it was stacked into."
    },
    {
      "name": "leather armor",
      "description": "Cracked but serviceable leather. Stiff from lying under a bedroll for years.",
      "kind": "armor",
      "armorClassBonus": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "health potion",
      "description": "A cloudy red liquid.",
      "kind": "consumable",
      "healAmount": 10
    },
    {
      "name": "clay flask",
      "description": "A small clay flask, wax over the stopper. It smells of resin and something green and bitter. The old woman at the cairn gave it away without being asked.",
      "kind": "consumable",
      "healAmount": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "apple",
      "description": "A shiny red apple with a small worm hole in the side.",
      "kind": "consumable",
      "healAmount": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "bone",
      "description": "A gnawed bone."
    },
    {
      "name": "shiny spoon",
      "description": "It is, unmistakably, a shiny spoon."
    },
    {
      "name": "key",
      "description": "A heavy iron key.",
      "isKey": true
    }
  ],
  "monsters": [
    {
      "name": "goblin",
      "description": "A goblin crouches in the corner, watching you. There is a shortsword across its knees, far too long for it.",
      "hitPoints": 7,
      "armorClass": 12,
      "attackStrength": 1,
      "attackDice": 6,
      "inventory": [
        "bone",
        "shortsword"
      ],
      "respawnSeconds": 300
    },
    {
      "name": "cave troll",
      "description": "A cave troll blocks the passage, breathing slowly.",
      "hitPoints": 20,
      "armorClass": 14,
      "attackStrength": 3,
      "attackDice": 8,
      "inventory": [
        "key"
      ],
      "respawnSeconds": 900
    },
    {
      "name": "drowned man",
      "description": "Something is standing in the black water at the foot of the stair, chest deep, with its back to you, not moving at all. When it turns round it is a man, or was one: swollen white, the eyes gone to milk, a rusted chisel still gripped in the right hand. He came down here to open that wall and the water had him first. He has not stopped trying.",
      "hitPoints": 14,
      "armorClass": 13,
      "attackStrength": 2,
      "attackDice": 6,
      "inventory": [
        "rusted chisel"
      ],
      "respawnSeconds": 600
    }
  ],
  "locations": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "name": "The Hollow",
      "description": "You stand in a shallow hollow ringed by pale stones. The air is still.",
      "connections": {
        "north": 2,
        "east": 3,
        "west": 6
      },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "hollow-stones",
          "triggers": [
            "*stones*",
            "*stone*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "The stones are cold and older than the hollow. Something was written here once, too large to read from down here."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "name": "Cave Mouth",
      "description": "The hollow narrows into a cave mouth. Cold air spills out of it.",
      "connections": {
        "south": 1,
        "north": 4
      },
      "monster": "goblin",
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "goblin-look",
          "triggers": [
            "*goblin*",
            "*creature*",
            "*it*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Knee high to you and mostly elbows, grey-green, with a face like a clenched hand. It keeps to the corner and it keeps its eyes on your hands rather than your face, which is the habit of something that has been kicked by bigger things all its life and has learned where the trouble comes from.\n\nIt is not guarding anything. It is not a puzzle. It has a bone it has been working on and a sword it cannot properly lift, and it is between you and the cave.\n\nIf the corner is empty as you read this, then you have already killed it, and the cave is making another one. It always has."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "goblin-sword",
          "triggers": [
            "*sword*",
            "*blade*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "The shortsword is not on the floor. It is across the goblin's knees, and it stays there while the goblin does — there is no taking it off a living thing in this valley, only off a dead one. That is a short walk from here and it costs what it costs.\n\nIf there is no goblin in the corner, then somebody has already had it away: look at the ground, and look in your own hands before you look anywhere else."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "name": "Old Camp",
      "description": "An abandoned camp. A firepit, long cold, and a scattering of belongings.",
      "connections": {
        "west": 1
      },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "camp-search",
          "once": true,
          "scope": "player",
          "triggers": [
            "*firepit*",
            "*belongings*",
            "*camp*",
            "*ashes*",
            "*search*",
            "*dig*",
            "*sift*",
            "*rummage*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Sifting through the ashes, you turn up a potion and a spoon."
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "addItems",
              "parameters": [
                "health potion",
                "shiny spoon"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "camp-bedroll",
          "once": true,
          "scope": "player",
          "triggers": [
            "*firepit*",
            "*belongings*",
            "*camp*",
            "*ashes*",
            "*bedroll*",
            "*armor*",
            "*armour*",
            "*again*",
            "*search*",
            "*dig*",
            "*sift*",
            "*rummage*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "You go through it a second time, and this time you drag the flattened bedroll aside. Folded underneath and gone stiff with damp: a set of cracked leather armor. Whoever camped here took it off to sleep and never put it back on."
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "addItems",
              "parameters": [
                "leather armor"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "camp-fire",
          "once": true,
          "scope": "player",
          "triggers": [
            "*fire*",
            "*rest*",
            "*sleep*",
            "*warm*",
            "*sit*",
            "*nap*",
            "*burn*",
            "*light*",
            "*camp*",
            "*ashes*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "You rake the firepit over and find one coal still alive at the bottom of it. Fed with a broken tent pole and a fistful of dry grass it stands up into a real fire, and the camp goes warm and orange around you. You put your back to the rock and let it work on you until the ache is out of your bones.\n\nIt burns down to nothing while you sleep. There is not enough left here to light twice."
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "heal",
              "parameters": [
                "full"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "camp-ashes",
          "triggers": [
            "*fire*",
            "*rest*",
            "*sleep*",
            "*warm*",
            "*sit*",
            "*nap*",
            "*burn*",
            "*light*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "The fire you made is ash again and there is nothing dry left to burn. You sit with it a while anyway. The cold comes up out of the floor."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "name": "The Deep Passage",
      "description": "The passage runs deep into the rock. Far ahead, something shifts.\n\nThere is a second way out of here, in the east wall. Not a crack: a doorway, squared off, with a lintel stone laid across the top of it and steps going down into the dark beyond. Whoever made the door at the far end of this passage made this as well, and made it first.",
      "connections": {
        "south": 2,
        "north": 5,
        "east": 8
      },
      "monster": "cave troll",
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "troll-look",
          "triggers": [
            "*troll*",
            "*creature*",
            "*monster*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Grey as the passage wall and hard to pick out from it until it moves, which it does slowly and only when it has decided to. Twice your weight. The hide across its shoulders has been opened and closed so many times it is more scar than skin, and none of those were made by anything with hands.\n\nOn a cord round its neck, a heavy iron key. It does not appear to know what the key is for. It only knows it is the key's.\n\nIf the passage is empty as you read this, then it is dead and the rock is quietly getting on with another one. They have never yet failed to come back."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "passage-down",
          "triggers": [
            "down",
            "go down",
            "*descend*",
            "*downward*",
            "*downwards*",
            "*stair*",
            "*stairs*",
            "*steps*",
            "*doorway*",
            "*lintel*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "You duck under the lintel and go down the cut steps. The air changes on the third one: older, and wet."
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "changeLocation",
              "parameters": [
                "8"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "name": "The Door",
      "description": "A heavy door, banded in iron, set into the living rock. It is the only thing down here that was made rather than found, and it does not belong to the cave: whatever is on the other side of it is not more cave.",
      "connections": {
        "south": 4
      },
      "isExit": true,
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "door-lock",
          "triggers": [
            "*open*",
            "*unlock*",
            "*door*",
            "*key*",
            "*push*",
            "*pull*",
            "*knock*",
            "*handle*",
            "*lock*",
            "*outside*",
            "*beyond*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Shoulder and weight do nothing. The lock wants iron — one heavy key, of the kind the troll in the passage keeps on a cord.\n\nTo anyone holding it the door gives at once, swinging in on cold daylight and a road going down through scrub and out of sight. That is the edge of everything built here, and going through it is the end of you: not a death, but the other ending, the one you walk to on your own feet and carrying your own gear. Nobody comes back in.\n\nThe word is exit. It will say all this to you once more before it takes you."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "name": "The Overlook",
      "description": "A ledge above the hollow. From here the pale stones make a pattern. Behind you the rock goes on up, broken into steps by frost — a scramble rather than a climb, and the moss on it has been torn by somebody's boots.",
      "connections": {
        "south": 1,
        "north": 7
      },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "overlook-edge",
          "triggers": [
            "*east*",
            "*edge*",
            "*jump*",
            "*over the side*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "The ledge goes east with you for two paces and then stops. Below the lip it is forty feet of nothing down onto the pale stones, and you would arrive among them in the manner of a dropped plate.\n\nBut stand at the lip and the whole valley is one thing at last. The hollow with its word laid out in it, exactly the size of a word. The black slot of the cave mouth. The camp off past it, its firepit gone grey. And the rock the door is set into at the far end is the same rock you have your boots on — the cave does not go anywhere. It goes under this hill and comes out the other side of it.\n\nThere is no east from here. There is down, and the way down is south, on your feet."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "overlook-pattern",
          "triggers": [
            "*pattern*",
            "*stones*",
            "*stone*",
            "*read*",
            "*hollow*",
            "*writing*",
            "*word*",
            "*down*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Seen from up here the pale stones are not scattered at all. They are letters, worn nearly flat, and the word they make is TOGETHER. Beneath it, scratched later and by a smaller hand: the troll keeps the key, and one pair of hands is enough to carry it out. Enough, it says, was never the same thing as well."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "overlook-climb",
          "triggers": [
            "climb*",
            "*scramble*",
            "*clamber*",
            "up",
            "go up",
            "up the rock",
            "*higher*",
            "*upward*",
            "*upwards*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "You get your hands into the frost-broken rock and go up it. It is steeper than it looks and easier than it looks, and it is over in a minute."
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "changeLocation",
              "parameters": [
                "7"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "name": "The Cairn",
      "description": "The rock gives out into a flat crown of hill and the wind has it all to itself. A cairn of grey stone stands here shoulder-high, and it is full of things: a boot, a comb, a snapped arrow, a tin cup, a dozen small objects wedged into the gaps and gone green with weather. An old woman sits on the lee side of it with her hands in her sleeves. She watches you arrive and does not get up.\n\nWedged into the stones, lately:\na shiny spoon, left by Gavin.\na shiny spoon, left by Haley.",
      "connections": {
        "south": 6
      },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-trade",
          "once": true,
          "scope": "player",
          "ifCarrying": [
            "shiny spoon"
          ],
          "triggers": [
            "*spoon*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "You offer it up. She turns it over twice, works it into a gap in the cairn at about knee height and thumbs a stone down over it.\n\n'That's yours in there now,' she says, and says your name over it once, the way you would over a grave, and then does not say it again. 'Everything in this heap was carried up by somebody who then went down that cave. Most of them I never saw come back. It isn't much of a grave and it isn't much of a shop, but it's what I keep, and the next one up this hill will see your name on it before they see me.'\n\nFrom inside her coat she brings out a small clay flask with wax over the stopper and puts it in your hand without being asked. 'Resin and bitterroot. It will close a wound, the once. Don't save it for a better day. There isn't a better day.'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "removeItems",
              "parameters": [
                "shiny spoon"
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "inscribe",
              "parameters": [
                "Wedged into the stones, lately:",
                "a shiny spoon, left by {name}.",
                "6"
              ]
            },
            {
              "action": "addItems",
              "parameters": [
                "clay flask"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-spoon-said",
          "triggers": [
            "*spoon*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "'A spoon,' she says. 'One each and one only — that's the whole of my trade, and I'd not do it twice for the same pair of hands.'\n\nShe looks down the valley, east past the cave mouth, to where the old camp sits with its firepit gone grey. 'If you haven't got one yet, there was one in those ashes the last time anybody went through them.'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-market",
          "triggers": [
            "*trade*",
            "*sell*",
            "*buy*",
            "*merchant*",
            "*shop*",
            "*coin*",
            "*gold*",
            "*money*",
            "*price*",
            "*worth*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "'There's no coin in this valley and I wouldn't give you any if there were,' she says. 'Keep your iron. You'll want the iron.' She looks at your hands. 'But a spoon — nobody has ever once needed a spoon down that hole, and one has come up this hill in more than one pocket. Name it and I'll take it off you.'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-wall",
          "triggers": [
            "*wall*",
            "*barrow*",
            "*chisel*",
            "*drowned*",
            "*water*",
            "*stair*",
            "*sunken*",
            "*deep*",
            "*below*",
            "*under*",
            "*fall of stone*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Her hands come out of her sleeves for the first time.\n\n'So you found the steps. Good. That door at the end of the passage is not the oldest thing in this valley and it never was — the stair is, and what's shut up at the bottom of it is older than me by a long way.'\n\nShe settles back. 'I'll tell you what I know, which is what I've watched. They go down there with a chisel and they get one stone out of that wall and then they go, one way or the other. Not one of them has ever got two. It isn't the stone that beats them, it's the hour, and the water, and the fact that a person only has the one life to spend on it.'\n\n'But the stones stay out,' she says. 'That's the thing. Whatever you take out of that wall is out of it for good, and the next one down finds your work waiting and starts from where you stopped. There's a word laid out in the hollow that people have been reading as advice for a long while. It was never advice. Go and open that wall and you'll see what it was.'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-refuse",
          "triggers": [
            "*give*",
            "*offer*",
            "*hand*",
            "*swap*",
            "*barter*",
            "*take this*",
            "*have this*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "She barely looks at it. 'One thing I'll take off you, and I've told you what it is. A spoon — and only because nobody in the history of this valley has ever needed a spoon down that hole. The rest of it you carry or you put down, same as everybody.'\n\nShe tips her chin at the cairn. 'Adding to that is a different matter. Nobody's ever asked permission and I've never refused it.'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-keeper",
          "triggers": [
            "*talk*",
            "*hello*",
            "hi",
            "*greet*",
            "*hail*",
            "*woman*",
            "*keeper*",
            "*hermit*",
            "*crone*",
            "*witch*",
            "*ask*",
            "*who*",
            "*name*",
            "*speak*",
            "*her*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "'You came up,' she says. 'Most don't. There's nothing up here and it's a bad wind.'\n\nShe does not give a name and does not seem to be waiting for anything. 'I keep the cairn. People go down that cave with everything they own, and they come back up with a key, or they don't come back up.'\n\nShe nods at the pale stones down in the hollow — the ones that spell TOGETHER when you look at them from the ledge. 'Two people put those there. I have watched this valley a long time and I have never yet seen two of you in it on the same day. You all come through it alone and you all do the same brave stupid thing alone, and then the ones who live walk out of that door and I never find out which.'\n\nShe puts a hand flat on the stones beside her. 'This is the nearest it gets. You'll meet nobody here, but you are not the first up this hill and you will not be the last, and what's wedged in this heap is the only post between you. Leave something in it and the next one reads your name. That's the whole of it. It has had to do.'\n\nShe is quiet a moment. 'That, and the wall at the bottom of the sunken stair. Ask me about that one and I'll talk longer than you want.'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-stones",
          "triggers": [
            "*cairn*",
            "*pile*",
            "*heap*",
            "*stack*",
            "*boot*",
            "*comb*",
            "*arrow*",
            "*cup*",
            "*things*",
            "*search*",
            "*dig*",
            "*sift*",
            "*stone*",
            "*rock*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Boot, comb, snapped arrow, tin cup, a clay pipe, a horse the size of a thumb carved out of soft wood, a ring of wire. None of it is worth anything. All of it was carried a long way. The stones are stacked dry, without mortar, and the cairn is plainly older than the woman sitting against it.\n\n'The new ones are at knee height, where I can reach,' she says. 'Those I can still put a name to. Look at the heap itself and you'll have them.'\n\n'Leave it,' she adds, without heat. 'Adding to it is allowed. The other thing isn't.'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cairn-sit",
          "triggers": [
            "*sit*",
            "*rest*",
            "*sleep*",
            "*nap*",
            "*wait*",
            "*stay*",
            "*wind*",
            "*view*",
            "*valley*",
            "*look out*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "You sit down on the lee side with the cairn at your back and the old woman on your left, and she says nothing else at all.\n\nThe valley lies there being empty: the hollow with its word in it, the dark slot of the cave mouth, the cold camp off to the east. Nothing in you closes over — a wound wants more than company — but you stay a while, and you get up less alone than you sat down."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "name": "The Sunken Stair",
      "description": "Twenty steps cut square out of the rock, going down, and the last six of them are under water. The water is black and flat and colder than the air above it; at the bottom it comes to your knees and no further, and it does not move at all, even when you do.\n\nThe stair ends at a fall of stone. It is not a collapse. The blocks are cut square and they were stacked into the opening on purpose, from this side, by somebody who meant it to stay shut — and then time leaned on them and left gaps a hand will go into and nothing else.\n\nBeside the wall, cut small and neat into the rock at shoulder height: TOGETHER. Under the word, two tally marks. Under the tallies, nothing.",
      "connections": {
        "west": 4
      },
      "monster": "drowned man",
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "fall-open-look",
          "if": [
            "fall-open"
          ],
          "triggers": [
            "*fall*",
            "*wall*",
            "*stone*",
            "*stones*",
            "*block*",
            "*blocks*",
            "*dig*",
            "*clear*",
            "*haul*",
            "*pry*",
            "*chisel*",
            "*gap*",
            "*rubble*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
