              "parameters": [
                "You lift it off them. It comes away easily; it was laid on, not buried with, and there is a difference, and whoever laid it knew there was.\n\nIt is a better blade than anything in this valley. The grip is horn and it is worn into the shape of a hand that was not the hand of the person on this slab — it is worn to the other one's grip, the one who walked out. They carried their own knife down here, and put it on their friend, and then went up that stair and out through the door and across the whole valley unarmed, past the troll, past the goblin, with nothing.\n\nThere is nothing else in this room worth taking and the knife is only here because it was meant to be found eventually. Take it out into the light. That is the errand."
              ]
