                "He is not old. Whatever is in this water, it keeps things — his boots are still boots and the chisel in his fist is still iron. He came down that stair with a tool and a plan and no light and he did not come back up, and there is no cairn for him and no name on anything and the woman on the hill never knew, because she only ever counted the ones who walked past her going out.\n\nHe will keep. Take the chisel off him: he came here to open that wall and you cannot do anything for him that is closer to the point.\n\nIf the water is empty as you read this, then you have already dealt with him, and the valley is quietly getting on with another one of him, which is the thing about this valley."
