    {
      "index": 9,
      "name": "The Long Barrow",
      "description": "A low chamber, dry as paper, with the sound of the water shut off behind you. The walls are the same cut stone as the thing you took apart to get in here, which means this room was built, in the dark, at the bottom of a flooded stair, by hand.\n\nOne person lies here. Laid out straight on a slab with their hands folded and a cloak drawn up under the chin, gone to dust along every edge. There is a lamp set by the head with the oil long dried out of it, a cup, a comb with two teeth missing, and a long knife in a sheath laid down the length of the body like a third arm.\n\nSomebody took a very long time over this, and then went back out through the doorway and stacked it shut behind them, from the other side, alone.",
