        {
          "interactionId": "barrow-word",
          "triggers": [
            "*together*",
            "*word*",
            "*hollow*",
            "*stones*",
            "*tally*",
            "*tallies*",
            "*why*",
            "*understand*",
            "*mean*"
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "Here is what the word in the hollow was.\n\nTwo people came into this valley, at the same time, which has not happened since. They laid pale stones out on the floor of the hollow big enough to be read from the ledge, and the word they laid was TOGETHER, and everybody who has read it since has read it as advice — as a sign left for strangers, telling them how to survive this place.\n\nIt was not advice. It was not addressed to you at all. It was two people writing down what they were, in letters the size of a house, because they were happy and there was nobody else in the world to tell.\n\nThen one of them died, and the other one built this room around them at the bottom of a flooded stair, and sealed it, and walked out of that door on their own, and the word was still lying up there in the sun meaning something completely different, and there was nothing to be done about that either.\n\nIt has been read as advice ever since by people who came here alone. Four of them have now taken a stone out of that wall to get in here and read it, one each, none of them ever meeting, across more lives than any of them had.\n\nWhich is not what the word said. But it is not nothing, and it may be the nearest this valley gets."
              ]
            }
          ]
